# No Cursor commit trailers

When you create commits, edit messages, or suggest `git commit` text (including multi-line bodies):

- Do **not** include `Made-with: Cursor` or any line starting with `Made-with:`.
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or similar IDE-generated `Co-authored-by` trailers.
- If the tool or environment inserts those lines, **remove them** before the commit is finalized.

Prefer the repo’s `prepare-commit-msg` hook when documented (`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`). Downstream projects: install the portable hook from `docs/templates/consumer-gating/` (see `pn-core://reference/consumer-gating.md`). Repos that enforce this in CI will fail merges if those lines appear in **any** commit in the pull request or in the pushed commit message (including default squash text that repeats commit bodies).
